## zmath — Michal Ziulek (zig-gamedev)

- **Upstream:** https://github.com/zig-gamedev/zmath
- **License:** MIT
- **Author:** Michal Ziulek and zig-gamedev contributors

zimr's `src/math.zig` is a hard fork of `zmath` at version
0.11.0-dev (fingerprint `0xfd23d422bd223cc2` in the `build.zig.zon`
of the upstream at vendor time).  Hard fork: there is no
upstream-merge story — `math.zig` is edited freely like any
other zimr source file.  Only Zig-version-drift fixes have been
applied on top of the verbatim vendor; each such fix is marked
with a `// [zimr Z0]` comment so the diff from upstream stays
auditable.  zimr-specific additions (Vector2 support, the
quat/vec/scalar helpers zimr needs that zmath lacks) sit below
the verbatim section.

zmath provides the row-major SIMD `Vec` / `Mat` / `Quat` types,
matrix builders, quaternion operations, and scalar helpers that
the rest of zimr is built on.  Convention is unchanged from the
upstream: row-major matrices, row vectors, `mul(v, m)` treats
`v` as a row, `mul(A, B)` composes "apply A then B."

