## Dear ImGui — Omar Cornut (`@ocornut`)

- **Upstream:** https://github.com/ocornut/imgui
- **License:** MIT
- **Author:** Omar Cornut and Dear ImGui contributors

zimr's `src/ui.zig` is an immediate-mode UI module shaped by Dear
ImGui's API and behavioural conventions: the begin/end pair
pattern, ID hashing for widget identity, the `WantCaptureMouse`
/ `WantCaptureKeyboard` convention, columns and tables, child
windows, tab bars, drag-drop, plot widgets, the slider / drag /
input-text family.  Zig idioms diverge where C++ default
arguments are awkward (zimr uses option structs with defaults)
and where overloading would clutter (separate `slider`,
`sliderInt`, `sliderFloat3` instead of overloaded `Slider`).

No Dear ImGui C++ source is included in zimr; the influence is
at the design level — public function signatures, widget
semantics, the docs that explain why a widget behaves the way it
does.  Algorithmic equivalence to upstream is the goal in the
common cases; the upstream is the reference manual for what
"correct" means.

The MIT license text reproduced verbatim:

