## BoundedArray — Jacob Young (`jedisct1`) and Zig contributors

- **Upstream:** Zig standard library (was `std.BoundedArray`)
- **License:** MIT
- **Author:** Jacob Young (`jedisct1`) and the Zig contributors

`BoundedArray` and `BoundedArrayAligned` in `src/utils.zig` are
vendored from upstream Zig's standard library.  BoundedArray
moved out of `std` during the 0.16 development cycle; zimr needs
a fixed-capacity inline array with no allocator (used at minimum
by `UiContext.debug_log: BoundedArray(DebugEvent, 256)`), so the
implementation is reinstated here.  The code is largely verbatim;
only line-length wrapping was adjusted to fit zimr's 120-column
convention.

The MIT license text is reproduced at the top of `src/utils.zig`
in the section comment that introduces the BoundedArray block,
per the upstream license's notice-preservation clause.  For
completeness it is also reproduced here:

